{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"a5340fc763cabe30675ff70692b4c9d3e170a4fc678a65eb6df1ad770d2e30c0","digest":{"component_or_area":"git fetch timeout handling","key_entities":["src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py","src/rebar/opcert_service/workspace.py","src/rebar/_commands/init.py","rebar._snapshot.git_fetch.stall_abort_args()","rebar._snapshot.git_fetch.is_stall_abort()","http.lowSpeedLimit","http.lowSpeedTime","_GIT_TIMEOUT","_FETCH_TIMEOUT","tests/_stall_remote.py","tests/integration/test_init_fail_closed.py"],"problem_keywords":["throughput-keyed stall abort","git fetch timeout","low-speed abort","300s wall-clock bound","network stall detection"],"propositions":["Three git fetch call sites (gerrit_client, opcert_service/workspace, _commands/init) still use 300s wall-clock timeout without throughput-based stall detection, creating identical exposure to byte-starved transfers as the fixed snapshot path","The low-speed abort mechanism built in 12e4 (stall_abort_args and is_stall_abort) is module-public and snapshot-agnostic, enabling reuse across multiple call sites without duplication","Each of the three 300s fetch sites must splice stall_abort_args() before the git subcommand and include test coverage proving zero-byte remotes abort as stalls while dribbling remotes are not aborted","Moving stall abort arming into _init_probe.run_bounded_git rather than init.py itself avoids module size constraint violation while keeping init.py untouched"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787597182517341001,"uuid":"297e77f6-b485-4a17-b7fb-9d85f60a8ce4"}